WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.759
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 10, the season
finale – let’s have a look.

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:08.639
We begin in King’s Landing with Cersei and
Tommen and Margaery and the Sparrow suiting

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:13.650
up for the big trial, with sept bells tolling
in the background, an ominous calm before

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.889
the storm.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:19.050
Everyone comes to the Sept – the sparrows,
the Tyrells, Lancel and Kevan Lannister, the

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.170
lords and ladies of King’s Landing, though
suspiciously, Cersei and Tommen stay at the

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.520
Red Keep.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.120
The trial begins, and Loras submits to the
Faith, confesses his crimes of banging Renly,

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.680
and lying about it at trial, and as punishment,
he has to give up the Tyrell name, which pretty

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.730
much ends House Tyrell, cause while in the
books, Loras has brothers, the show-version

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.710
of Loras is apparently the only heir to their
house.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.650
The Sparrow’s goals aren’t just religious,
they’re political, he’s taking down the

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:49.330
great houses, so now that Tyrell’s gone,
he turns to Lannister, sending Lancel to go

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.450
get Cersei.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.700
Lancel, for some reason, decides to follow
a boy into a basement, where he gets stabbed

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.070
and discovers the wildfire set to blow up
the Sept.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.290
Meanwhile, Pycelle is lured to Qyburn’s
laboratory where he’s killed by little birds.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.450
In the books, it’s not Qyburn, but Varys
who does this – Varys murders Pycelle and

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:11.569
Kevan and gives this cool speech about how
he’s working to destabilise Westeros, to

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:16.220
make the Targaryen invasion easier – though
in the books he’s sorta supporting a different

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.450
Targaryen – it’s complicated – but the
point is that now Pycelle is dead.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:24.850
Back at the Sept, Marge suspects that something’s
up, so she tries to evacuate, but it’s too

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:25.850
late.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:29.670
Lancel tries to stop the wildfire but he’s
too slow too, so everything blows the fuck

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.990
up, killing the Sparrow, in his moment of
victory, and the Tyrells, in their moment

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:38.549
of defeat, killing Cersei’s own uncle, Kevan
Lannister and his son Lancel.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.599
And all these hundreds or thousands of others,
ladies and lords, sparrows, smallfolk, everyone

00:01:43.599 --> 00:01:46.580
in and around the Sept is killed by Cersei.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.899
How can she justify this terrible crime?

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:54.310
In the next scene, we see Cersei with Unella,
the shame bell lady, and Cersei says the reason

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:59.159
she killed all these people is “because
it felt good”, that imagining their shock

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:02.909
and pain is the greatest joy she’s ever
felt.

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:05.689
This is some Ramsay Bolton level evil here.

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:09.340
Previously when Cersei did terrible things,
she’d tell herself that the she did it to

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.599
protect her kids, but here she’s straight
up saying that she kills people for pleasure,

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:18.290
she’s turned to the Dark Side, and the Mountain
is the Darth Vader to her Emperor – she

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.129
sends him in torture Unella, and we get a
brief shot of the Mountain unmasked.

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:25.760
It’s hard to see in the dark, but Gregor
does pretty much look like Vader.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.730
Then we see Tommen, watching his city burn.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.280
He has a failed as a king by letting his people
die.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.180
He has failed as a husband by letting his
wife Margaery burn.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.850
He has failed as a follower of the Faith by
letting the Sparrow blow up.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.610
And of course none of this is really his fault.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:44.239
He’s always been a pawn of other players,
manipulated by the Sparrow, by Cersei, by

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:48.579
Margaery, he’s never really done anything
of his own will before, so this death is tragic

00:02:48.579 --> 00:02:53.310
not only because he was basically a good kid,
and that he never knew his real father, and

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.989
that his family mistreated him, its tragic
that deciding to die is like the first real

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:00.410
choice he’s ever made.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.090
The joke going round at the moment is that
this why they call it King’s Landing, cause

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:07.489
you know, the King landed…

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:09.840
All this stuff, by the way, will be very different
in the books.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.230
For starters the Tommen of the books is like
ten years old, his main activities are to

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:19.049
play with his kittens, and to try to outlaw
beets – book-Tommen won’t be jumping outta

00:03:19.049 --> 00:03:20.400
windows any time soon.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.019
The way it might go down in the books is that
Tommen might die some other way, then Cersei

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:27.469
will blow up the wildfire in response, in
grief and rage.

00:03:27.469 --> 00:03:31.000
Further, the wildfire in the books probably
won’t just blow up the Sept, in fact the

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.829
wildfire beneath the Sept was found and removed,
but there still is wildfire “all over the

00:03:35.829 --> 00:03:39.950
city” – so maybe it’ll be the whole
city that burns down.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.341
This may happen in the show too, somehow,
because we still have that vision of the Red

00:03:43.341 --> 00:03:48.530
Keep burned that hasn’t happened yet – maybe
it’ll be Dany’s dragonfire that sets it

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.530
off.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:50.530
Anyway.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.109
Over at the Twins, the Freys and Lannisters
celebrate the retaking of Riverrun.

00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:57.590
Jaime and Bronn chat, and then Walder comes
along and says he and Jaime aren’t so different,

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.909
you and I – they’re both Kingslayers – Walder
killed King Robb Stark at the Red Wedding,

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:06.319
and Jaime killed King Aerys Targaryen, during
Robert’s Rebellion twenty years ago.

00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:10.280
Both Walder and Jaime are hated for these
dishonourable killings, though what Walder

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.430
doesn’t know is that Jaime killed the Mad
King for a good reason, to stop Aerys blowing

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.400
up King’s Landing with wildfire – bit
like what Cersei just did.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.950
Jaime doesn’t want to be like Walder.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.370
He increasingly tries to be a good, honourable
person – so it’ll be interesting to see

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.510
how he reacts to Cersei’s wildfire attack.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.720
Cersei sees the dead body of her last son.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.950
And it’s just like the gypsy woman said
– Maggy the Frog prophesied that all Cersei’s

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:39.020
children would die – gold their crowns,
and gold their shrouds, and it all came true.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.190
So maybe the reason Cersei takes the death
of her son so calmly is that she already knew

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:48.190
it was going to happen, she’d already grieved
and now she’s numb, empty, with nothing

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:53.080
left in the world to give her joy, except
the suffering of her enemies.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.320
Another part of the prophecy in the books
is that Cersei will be replaced by a “younger

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:00.380
and more beautiful queen” – Cersei thought
this was Margaery, but it’s probably gonna

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.070
be Dany.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.160
In the Reach, Sam and Gilly arrive at the
city of Oldtown, that lighthouse there is

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.220
called the Hightower, they’re not creative
with names here.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:13.380
They go to the Citadel, home of the maesters,
they deal with some annoying bureaucrat, and

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.290
then Sam’s let into the library.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.571
Reading is one of Sam’s few loves, and this
is the biggest library in Westeros, maybe

00:05:19.571 --> 00:05:23.480
in the world, so this is a dream come true
for Samwell Tarly.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.080
Of course it’ll also be important to the
plot – maybe Sam will find some book about

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.370
white walkers or Azor Ahai or Valyrian steel,
something that could help the humans win the

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.460
war gainst the walkers.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.340
Also that astrolabey thing at the ceiling
is the thing from the intro of the show, showing

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.400
the history of Westeros.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.500
But yeah while Sam is reading, it’s not
clear what Gilly and her baby will do, because

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.400
the Citadel doesn’t accept women and children.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.820
In the books, there’s heaps of other stuff
going down here, like, the Faceless Man Jaqen

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.240
H’ghar comes disguised as an alchemist to
steal a book, and one of the Sand Snakes comes

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.820
disguised as a man to study, and later ironborn
raiders under Euron arrive, and there’s

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:01.920
also this enigmatic maester called Marywn
the Mage doing some spooky magic stuff, he

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.120
might be the archmaester this guy mentions.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:07.170
So we don’t know how much of this will make
into the show, but there’s certainly lots

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.480
of cool content to draw from the books.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:13.551
One likely conflict in the show is that Sam’s
father Randyll may come for his Valyrian steel

00:06:13.551 --> 00:06:17.020
sword Heartsbane, which we see Sam still has.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:21.690
Up at Winterfell, Jon complains to Mel about
having to sit at the back at family feasts.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:25.330
Mel tells him to check his privilege – she
grew up as a slave, at least in the books

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.930
– she’s still haunted by nightmares of
her childhood – and her original name, by

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.290
the way, was Melony.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.600
Then Davos arrives and confronts Mel about
the murder of Shireen.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:38.580
Mel admits that she did it, admits she was
wrong, but argues that Jon should keep her

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.620
anyway cause she’ll be useful in the war
against the walkers.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.700
Which is a really good point – Mel is one
of the only people who seems to know what

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.710
the deal is with the war for the dawn and
Azor Ahai and all that, but regardless, Jon

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:52.380
decides to exile Mel, orders her to “ride
south”.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.680
Which could go in some interesting ways – at
the same time Mel heads south, the brotherhood

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.920
without banners is heading north – Thoros
is a red priest, like Mel, and in the show

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:00.980
they’ve met before.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:05.250
Maybe they’ll catch up, talk about their
god, and Jon’s resurrection and stuff.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:08.190
Brienne and Pod are also heading north, and
they get caught up with the brotherhood in

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.190
the books.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:13.120
Arya’s also around – when Mel meets her
in Season 3, she says they’ll meet again.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:18.940
So all of these characters could be somehow
involved in whatever comes next for Melisandre.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:23.030
Jon and Sansa talk, and she apologises for
not telling Jon about the knights of the Vale

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.740
before the Battle of the Bastards.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.310
She doesn’t explain why she didn’t tell
him – even though it was kind of a big deal

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:32.780
strategically – but he accepts her apology
– of course, he should be apologising too

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:36.810
– he almost got everyone killed by riding
into the middle of battle instead of sticking

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:42.030
to the plan with the trenches, so really both
Sansa and Jon were pretty dumb last episode.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:45.380
The point of this scene, though, seems to
be to show some tension and uneasiness between

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.550
Jon and Sansa – it’s not certain if they’ll
trust each other – which could lead to conflict

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:50.550
next season.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:56.320
Also, a white raven arrives to signify that
winter has officially finally come – and

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.590
it only took six seasons.

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:00.330
Olenna Tyrell comes to Dorne.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.100
She wants revenge on Cersei for killing her
family, so she allies with the Sand Snakes,

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.640
who also hate the Lannisters for the deaths
of Oberyn and Elia.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.690
Then Varys walks in, representing Daenerys,
and they form a powerful three way alliance

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.510
between Targaryen, Tyrell and Martell.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.960
Of course the Sand Snakes aren’t really
Martells, they’re illegitimate bastards

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.780
who murdered the rightful Lord Doran Martell.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:25.270
And Olenna isn’t really a Tyrell, she’s
a Redwyne who married a Tyrell, so she probably

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.980
shouldn’t be in power either.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.320
The politics here don’t really strictly
make sense, but the overall idea of this alliance

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:35.890
is cool and sets the stage for Daenerys to
invade.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:38.190
In Meereen, Daenerys breaks up with Daario.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:42.190
She can’t bring a lover to Westeros, because
politically, she needs to open for marriage.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:46.880
Daario is to stay and keep the peace in Meereen,
which seems like a bad idea.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.720
Daario’s a random mercenary.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.370
He doesn’t know how to govern, and he doesn’t
care about Meereen.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.190
And the situation here is still far from okay,
right?

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:58.440
Dany has banned slavery and cast down the
masters, but there’s no new system to take

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.550
its place.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:03.420
The Sons of the Harpy are still out there,
and the freed slaves still need protection.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.630
But Daenerys decides to declare Mission Accomplished
and roll on out anyway.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:11.580
She renames Slaver’s Bay to the Bay of Dragons,
which is cool, but you could call North Korea

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.120
Freedom Land, and that wouldn’t make it
true.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:18.090
Conquering a foreign land, destroying the
existing social structure, then leaving, can

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.980
have very bad results.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:24.210
One of the major themes of the books is the
messiness and moral complexity of war, and

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:28.750
for the show to capture this, it should revisit
Meereen later to show us the chaos Dany’s

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.570
leaving behind her.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:35.020
On a lighter note, who are the eligible bachelors
of Westeros Dany might marry?

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:38.420
Maybe Jaime – now that he’s been released
from his Kingsguard vows, he’s presumably

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:43.150
the heir to House Lannister and all its power,
and Jaime might not be keen on Cersei now

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:47.360
that she’s a mass murderer and all – so
maybe Dany’ll hook up with Goldenhand – only

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:50.110
catch might be that he killed her dad.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:54.180
A better candidate could be Jon – as the
King in the North, he controls a huge chunk

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.180
of Westeros.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:59.840
He’s also supposedly Azor Ahai, the prophesied
saviour of the world, just as she is, and

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.480
he kinda represents Ice, in the same way Dany
represents Fire and the books series is called

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:09.940
A Song of Ice and Fire, so basically Jon and
Dany could make a hell of a power couple.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:14.100
The only reason why it probably won’t happen
is that it almost feels too obvious.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:18.950
Dany talks with Tyrion, and he swears himself
to her service, seems truly devoted to her

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:19.950
cause.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:24.140
Which seems kinda sudden, almost out of character
– Tyrion’s hardly the kneeling type, and

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.600
in the books he’s cynical about this whole
Targaryen restoration business.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.410
But it does kinda make sense that he’d be
drawn to Dany.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:34.330
Tyrion’s just lost his family, and his lover,
he’s far from home, what he needs now is

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.400
purpose.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.990
And back in Westeros, that was politics.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:41.860
Being Hand of the King made him feel valuable
and important, so when Daenerys makes him

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:44.370
her Hand, that’s exactly what Tyrion needs.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.810
Same goes for a lot of Dany’s followers.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:50.400
She draws all these misfits and exiles and
broken men to her, people who need a flag

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.190
to follow, something to believe in.

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:56.040
She offers them hope for a brighter future,
so they fight for her.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.860
And historically, that’s never gone badly,
right?

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:03.730
Then we see Arya infiltrate the Twins disguised
with the face of a serving girl.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:09.040
She makes a pie out of Black Walder and Lothar
Frey, and feeds it to their father, Walder

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:12.980
who she then kills to avenge the deaths of
her mother and brother at the Red Wedding.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.960
Fans have pointed out that the three men who
arranged the Red Wedding – Walder Frey,

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.070
Tywin Lannister, and Roose Bolton – are
killed in the same way their victims are – Walder

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:25.170
has his throat slashed, like Catelyn, Tywin
is shot with a crossbow, like Robb, and Roose

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:28.480
is stabbed in the gut, just like Talisa, so
there’s a cool symmetry there.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:34.270
But yeah Arya has made another kill, she watches
and smiles as the man before her dies, and

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.680
it’ll be interesting to see how the show
plays Arya’s arc in the future.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:41.210
Like, are we meant to cheer as this child
dedicates her life to a murder spree?

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:44.550
Or should we question whether violent vengeance
is the only answer?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:48.860
But for now, there are still targets left
on Arya’s list – she’s killed Polliver,

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:53.260
Meryn Trant, and now Walder Frey, but there’s
still Cersei and Gregor Clegane, so maybe

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.710
Arya’ll go after them.

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:58.520
But there were others who were on her list
temporarily – the Hound, for killing Mycah,

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:02.839
Beric and Thoros and Melisandre for betraying
Gendry – and all these guys are currently

00:12:02.839 --> 00:12:07.250
in and around the riverlands – so maybe
something’ll happen with them.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:11.850
Back at Winterfell, Sansa meets with Littlefinger,
in the same spot Ned and Cat meet in Season

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:12.850
1.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:16.060
Littlefinger says that his ultimate goal is
become the King of Westeros, with Sansa at

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.060
his side.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.880
Which pretty much fits with what we’ve seen
of him so far – he’s always been hungry

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:24.000
for power, and he’s always wanted Sansa
– mostly cause she reminds him of her mum,

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.530
who Littlefinger loved.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:29.400
But Sansa rejects him – she knows that he’s
only really out for himself – but she also

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:32.670
doesn’t move against him which she probably
could and should.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.250
Cause Littlefinger’s a seriously bad dude,
right?

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.960
He killed Sansa’s aunt Lysa.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.130
He betrayed Ned Stark.

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:41.900
He caused the War of the Five Kings by turning
the Lannisters against the Starks.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.800
He even helped kill King Joffrey for what
that’s worth.

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:48.089
Littlefinger is dangerous and he’s worked
against the Starks.

00:12:48.089 --> 00:12:51.500
And as the Lady of Winterfell, Sansa’s in
a position to take him down.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:55.000
She could tell the knights of the Vale that
Littlefinger killed their Lady Lysa, and lied

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.300
about the Boltons.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:59.650
She could tell the lords of the north that
Littlefinger betrayed their Lord Ned Stark,

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:01.740
though we don’t know how much Sansa knows
about that.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:06.170
Either way, Sansa totally could get Littlefinger
imprisoned or executed for his crimes which

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:10.470
would make everybody much safer, but she doesn’t
– she lets him go.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:14.620
So, while Sansa doesn’t team up with Littlefinger
here, she’s leaves that door open, keeps

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:18.360
him as possible ally in the future – which
could be really useful, but could also go

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:24.040
very badly, cause as Sansa says herself, only
a fool would trust Littlefinger.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:28.089
Beyond the Wall, Benjen drops off Bran and
Meera by a weirwood tree – the same tree

00:13:28.089 --> 00:13:31.560
Jon and Sam swear their Night’s Watch vows
at in Season 1.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.230
Benjen says he can’t take them through the
Wall itself, because the Wall has magic that

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.339
stops zombies like him from going through
– which is the same deal as the book character

00:13:39.339 --> 00:13:40.339
Coldhands.

00:13:40.339 --> 00:13:43.649
The worrying thing is that these spells that
protect the Wall are probably the magic of

00:13:43.649 --> 00:13:47.480
the children of the forest – the same kinda
magic that protected Bloodraven’s cave until

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:51.470
that magic was broken by the Night King’s
psychic connection to Bran, and that mark

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.630
he made in Episode 5.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:57.880
Maybe the magic of the Wall could be broken
in some similar way.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:01.501
So anyway Benjen leaves, says he’ll do what
he can to fight the white walkers, and Bran

00:14:01.501 --> 00:14:05.120
turns to the weirwood tree, says that’s
he’s the three-eyed raven now – and again

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.470
we still don’t really know what that means
exactly, but it involves these visions he

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:10.630
has through the weirwood trees.

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:15.010
And then we get one of the most anticipated
moments in the series – Bran has a vision

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.000
of the birth of Jon Snow.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:21.830
We see young Ned Stark at the Tower of Joy,
seeing his sister Lyanna in a “bed of blood”,

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.930
just having given birth to Jon.

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:28.430
This finally proves that Jon is not the bastard
son of Ned and some unknown woman, but is

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.470
actually the son of his sister Lyanna.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.830
Now, the episode doesn’t make clear who
the father is, but we know from hints in the

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:39.120
books and the show, and from a frankly confusing
graph from HBO, that the father of Jon Snow

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.740
is Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:45.210
Rhaegar hasn’t appeared in the show, but
basically, he’s the older brother of Daenerys,

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.620
and the son of the Mad King Aerys.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:51.380
Some twenty years before the story starts,
Rhaegar ran off with Lyanna Stark, and this

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:55.720
started Robert’s Rebellion, the war that
killed Aerys and Rhaegar and made Robert the

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.340
King of Westeros.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:15:01.150
Robert hated Targaryens, he wanted to kill
them all, and that’s why Jon had to be hidden

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:06.570
– as the son of Rhaegar, Jon is half-Targaryen,
so Ned had to lie and say Jon was his bastard,

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:10.090
in order to protect him from Robert, that’s
what Lyanna is talking bout here –

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:14.420
But yeah the point of all this is that Jon
is the son of a Stark and a Targaryen, of

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.420
ice and fire.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:19.520
He’s the grandson of the Mad King, and the
nephew of Daenerys – which makes this potential

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.100
hookup kind of awkward.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.440
But this could have some huge implications
– this means that Jon could have a claim

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.630
on the Iron Throne – he is still a bastard,
if Lyanna and Rhaegar weren’t married, but

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:32.160
there are theories they could have had a secret
wedding – maybe Bran could have a vision

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.160
of that.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.700
Further, as a Targaryen, Jon might be able
to ride dragons like Daenerys.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:41.470
He might be fireproof like Daenerys – except
there was that one time he got burned – the

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:44.020
whole fireproof thing is confusing in the
show.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:48.660
But another big thing is that Azor Ahai, the
hero prophesied to save the world from darkness

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:54.810
is apparently meant to be from Aerys’ line
– so Jon now fits another part of this prophecy.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:16:00.040
Also, Ned leans Arthur Dayne’s famous sword,
called Dawn, against Lyanna’s bed, which

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.740
kind of connects to another part of the Azor
Ahai prophecy, saying he’ll be born beneath

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:06.560
a bleeding star.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:10.150
Dawn is loosely connected to stars, and it’s
literally covered in blood.

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:14.170
So yeah, basically, more evidence that Jon
is Game of Thrones Jesus.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:19.360
The real tricky question is how Jon, and the
rest of Westeros, will find out about his

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:20.360
parentage.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:23.700
Bran could tell Jon, but the rest of Westeros
will want proof before they let him sit the

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:25.410
Iron Throne or whatever.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:29.140
And there are a few ways this could happen
– maybe Howland Reed, the other survivor

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:30.910
of the Tower of Joy, could turn up.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.779
Maybe there’s some kind of secret hidden
still in the Winterfell crypts.

00:16:33.779 --> 00:16:35.110
We’ll have to wait and see.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:40.910
But at least we now the truth – that Jon
is a son of ice and fire.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:45.250
At Winterfell, the northern lords declare
Jon the King in the North, the White Wolf,

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.620
just as Robb Stark was the Young Wolf.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.200
And this is super cool, though it doesn’t
make much sense.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:54.459
Like, sure, Jon was brave at the Battle of
the Bastards, but he’s also a deserter of

00:16:54.459 --> 00:16:57.020
the Night’s Watch, which is punishable by
death.

00:16:57.020 --> 00:17:00.360
And he let wildlings through the Wall, which
most of the north hates.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:04.240
And he’s a bastard, not the Lord of Winterfell
– Sansa is the rightful ruler.

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:08.159
And half these lords weren’t at the battle,
they’ve never met Jon before – so why

00:17:08.159 --> 00:17:10.939
do they all love him and trust him so much?

00:17:10.939 --> 00:17:14.549
If Jon becomes King in the North in the books,
it’ll happen a very different way – there’s

00:17:14.549 --> 00:17:19.069
this whole thing with Robb naming Jon his
heir, then sending Maege Mormont and Galbart

00:17:19.069 --> 00:17:22.839
Glover to Howland Reed so maybe in the books
those guys will turn up and reveal Robb’s

00:17:22.839 --> 00:17:25.720
wishes – but it’s probably fair that the
show simplifies this.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:30.870
The point is that Jon now rules a huge chunk
of Westeros, apparently including the Vale,

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:35.269
cause Littlefinger says he is sworn to House
Stark – but of course we know not to trust

00:17:35.269 --> 00:17:39.330
Littlefinger – he wants Sansa, not Jon,
in charge in the north, so we’ll likely

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.119
see some conflict between these guys next
season.

00:17:42.119 --> 00:17:45.710
Littlefinger may try to turn Sansa against
Jon.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:49.600
Then Jaime returns to King’s Landing, like
Troy in Community, and this is definitely

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.139
the darkest timeline.

00:17:51.139 --> 00:17:56.070
Cersei sits the Iron Throne, crowns herself
the ruler of Westeros, while her city still

00:17:56.070 --> 00:18:01.009
burns in the background, she’s gone full
Evil Queen here, this is some dark lord shit.

00:18:01.009 --> 00:18:05.519
She’s not the rightful ruler, she’s a
dictator, who seized power by blowing up everyone

00:18:05.519 --> 00:18:08.149
else – maybe you could call that right of
conquest.

00:18:08.149 --> 00:18:12.360
But this is not a stable regime – the people
will hate her – because she just blew up

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.990
the equivalent of the Vatican.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.929
She has no allies or army as far as we know.

00:18:16.929 --> 00:18:20.289
And the Tyrells, Martells and Targaryens are
allied against her.

00:18:20.289 --> 00:18:23.239
So this reign of terror probably won’t last
long.

00:18:23.239 --> 00:18:25.529
The interesting drama will be Jaime’s response.

00:18:25.529 --> 00:18:30.120
He’ll be having flashbacks to Aerys, the
Mad King he killed to protect the people,

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:34.350
if Jaime is to become the better person he’s
trying to be, maybe he’ll have to kill his

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:37.739
lifelong lover, this terrible new mad queen.

00:18:37.739 --> 00:18:42.190
Which, would, by the way, fulfil another part
of this prophecy, that Cersei would be killed

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.700
by her valonqar, or little brother.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.820
The episode ends with another much-anticipated
moment – Daenerys Targaryen finally sails

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:56.320
for Westeros, with a huge fleet, full of Unsullied,
and Dothraki, and ironborn, not to mention

00:18:56.320 --> 00:19:01.159
three dragons – she’s also got Varys,
and Tyrell and Martells ships, so this must

00:19:01.159 --> 00:19:04.380
be months after the rest of the episode cause
of the travel time.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:08.260
But, sidenote – this is the first time we’ve
seen Varys and Daenerys together, and they

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:12.950
actually have a lot to talk about, cause Varys
has been fucking with Daenerys’ life for

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:17.769
years – his scheming with Illyiro led to
Dany’s marriage with Khal Drogo.

00:19:17.769 --> 00:19:22.519
Varys informed on Dany to the small council,
and ordered an assassination attempt on her

00:19:22.519 --> 00:19:26.990
once – and Dany does know this, even in
the show, so she should have some tough questions

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:28.480
for the eunuch.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:31.809
Another little thing is that it’s weird
to see the Dothraki so comfortable at sea,

00:19:31.809 --> 00:19:34.591
when it’s kind of a thing that they’re
terrible sailors – maybe that’ll come

00:19:34.591 --> 00:19:35.591
up later.

00:19:35.591 --> 00:19:41.610
But this is a great way to end the season,
Daenerys is finally set to take the Throne.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.039
So let’s look at the situation at the end
of the season.

00:19:44.039 --> 00:19:48.619
On the Iron Throne, you’ve got Cersei Lannister,
with Qyburn and the Mountain at her side.

00:19:48.619 --> 00:19:52.299
Jaime’s there too, and he might do something
to stop her.

00:19:52.299 --> 00:19:56.169
Allied against her are the Tyrells, under
Olenna, and Dorne, under the Sand Snakes,

00:19:56.169 --> 00:20:00.259
who are supporting Daenerys Targaryen, sailing
in from the east with Tyrion and Varys and

00:20:00.259 --> 00:20:04.039
Missandei and Grey Worm and Yara and Theon
and an army.

00:20:04.039 --> 00:20:08.379
The King of the Iron Islands is Euron Greyjoy,
and he’ll probably be a big bad guy next

00:20:08.379 --> 00:20:12.850
season – remember he wants to kill Yara
and Theon, marry Dany and take over the world,

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:17.190
and in the books he has some schemes involving
black magic and dragons.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:21.649
Jon Snow is the King in the North, supported
by the northern houses and by Tormund’s

00:20:21.649 --> 00:20:25.320
wildlings, while Sansa is apparently still
the Lady of Winterfell.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:30.480
The north is supposedly supported by the Vale,
ruled in name by Robin Arryn, but in practice

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:33.739
by Littlefinger – who’ll probably also
be a big baddie next season.

00:20:33.739 --> 00:20:38.070
It’s not clear who rules the riverlands,
now that Walder Frey’s dead, but Edmure

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:41.289
Tully’s still alive, so maybe his power
could eventually restored.

00:20:41.289 --> 00:20:45.470
For now you’ve got Beric, Thoros, the Hound,
Brienne, Pod and Arya all travelling round

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.440
the riverlands, and Melisandre coming in from
the north so all sorts of stuff could happen

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:50.710
around there.

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:54.669
Down south Sam and Gilly are at Oldtown, and
Randyll and Dickon might come for them.

00:20:54.669 --> 00:21:00.289
Over in Essos, Meereen is left to Daario and
the Sons of the Harpy, and presumably Kinvara

00:21:00.289 --> 00:21:03.870
and the red priests are still there – kinda
weird they didn’t do much this season.

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:08.350
Jorah is wondering round Essos somewhere,
looking for a cure for his greyscale.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:11.720
Gendry is still rowing around somewhere as
well, presumably…

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:16.519
We might also see Tycho Nestoris again – remember
the Crown owes the Iron Bank a lot of money.

00:21:16.519 --> 00:21:22.059
But of course the biggest threat of all is
posed by the white walkers and their army

00:21:22.059 --> 00:21:23.059
of the dead.

00:21:23.059 --> 00:21:27.340
Dolorous Edd and the Wall probably can’t
stop them on his own, nor can Benjen, so Bran

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:29.179
and Meera better get south soon.

00:21:29.179 --> 00:21:33.750
So the big conflicts next season will probably
be Dany’s invasion against Cersei and maybe

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:37.970
Euron, there’ll be stuff in the north between
Jon and Sansa and Littlefinger, but above

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:43.370
all there’ll be the War for the Dawn, between
the white walkers and everybody else.

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:48.159
There are just two short seasons of Game of
Thrones left, like thirteen hours of content.

00:21:48.159 --> 00:21:51.350
This is the beginning of the end.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:55.749
So Game of Thrones Season 6 is done, but there
is still so much Thrones left to talk about,

00:21:55.749 --> 00:21:59.799
with theories, and analysis of characters
and plot, and predictions and speculation

00:21:59.799 --> 00:22:03.309
about the future of the series, and heaps
of stuff in the books that doesn't even appear

00:22:03.309 --> 00:22:04.309
in the show.

00:22:04.309 --> 00:22:08.409
So this is the kind of content you'll be seeing
from Alt Shift X when we return in August

00:22:08.409 --> 00:22:12.740
– we’re taking a break for a while – the
Patreon will be paused so no one’ll be charged

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:13.740
for July.

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:16.320
But make sure to subscribe so you don’t
miss future videos – if you’d like to

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:20.139
be notified the moment videos come out, you
can press this bell button on the Alt Shift

00:22:20.139 --> 00:22:22.730
X channel on the YouTube app on your phone.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:26.179
Also, if you haven’t read the books, now
is a really good time to start.

00:22:26.179 --> 00:22:30.179
The books are everything you love about the
Game of Thrones show, but more.

00:22:30.179 --> 00:22:34.789
More detail more depth, more complexity, more
drama, more politics, more mysteries, more

00:22:34.789 --> 00:22:39.809
magic, so many extra little connections and
relationships and backstories and side-characters

00:22:39.809 --> 00:22:42.109
and histories – the books are amazing.

00:22:42.109 --> 00:22:47.109
They aren't the easiest read – they are
dense and complex and very bloody long, but

00:22:47.109 --> 00:22:49.389
if you can get into em, you will really enjoy
em.

00:22:49.389 --> 00:22:53.509
So there's a link in the description to buy
the books – its an Amazon link that supports

00:22:53.509 --> 00:22:57.710
this channel if you use it at no extra cost
to you, otherwise you can find the books by

00:22:57.710 --> 00:22:59.610
other ways online.

00:22:59.610 --> 00:23:02.690
If you’ve already read the books and you
wanna go deeper down the rabbit hole, go check

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:07.649
out the Game of Thrones forums, like the Song
of Ice and Fire subreddit, and Westeros.org.

00:23:07.649 --> 00:23:12.019
Many of the ideas and theories discussed on
this channel come from these forums.

00:23:12.019 --> 00:23:16.070
Also the podcasts – there are heaps of great
Game of Thrones podcasts, two of the biggest

00:23:16.070 --> 00:23:19.700
and best are Radio Westeros and History of
Westeros.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:24.440
Really in-depth analysis of story, themes,
theories, predictions, so go and check them

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:25.440
out.

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:28.200
Between the podcasts and the forums and the
books and this channel, there is plenty of

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:32.429
Thrones content to last until next season
– and if we’re lucky we may even get a

00:23:32.429 --> 00:23:33.950
new book soon…

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:35.039
So thank you for watching.

00:23:35.039 --> 00:23:38.940
Thank you for commenting and liking and subscribing
and thank you for the emails and tweets and

00:23:38.940 --> 00:23:43.100
